Given : \text{E}^\theta_{\text{Ag}^+/\text{Ag}} = 0.80\text{ V}, \text{E}^\theta_{\text{Hg}_2^{2+}/\text{Hg}} = 0.79\text{ V}, \text{E}^\theta_{\text{Cu}^{2+}/\text{Cu}} = 0.24\text{ V} \text{ and } \text{E}^\theta_{\text{Mg}^{2+}/\text{Mg}} = -2.37\text{ V}

Statement (I) : With increasing voltage, the sequence of deposition of metals on the cathode will be \text{Ag}, \text{Hg} and \text{Cu}

Statement (II) : Magnesium will not be deposited at cathode instead oxygen gas will be evolved at the cathode.

